## A note on the third-party material in this repository

The MIT licence above covers the **source code of this project** — `app/`, `tests/`,
`tools/`, `src-tauri/`, `build.py` and the documentation.

It does **not** cover, and this project does not claim any rights over:

- **`app/vendor/js-yaml.js`** — the bundled YAML parser, which is MIT licensed in its own right
  and is included so the built app needs no network. Its own licence header is intact in the file.
- **`data/sources/*/Evt/`** — the WCH EVT packages: the vendor's Standard Peripheral Library,
  startup code, linker scripts and examples. These belong to WCH and are present as the
  documentary authority the generated code is verified against. They are **not** redistributed as
  a usable SDK, and PlatformIO installs the real SDK separately as
  `framework-wch-noneos-sdk`.
- **`data/sources/*/Datasheets/`** — WCH datasheets and reference manuals, likewise, and likewise
  not ours. They are here so that every fact in `data/mcus/*.yaml` can be traced to the page it
  came from.
- **`data/packages/packages.yaml`** — package geometries (SOP, TSSOP, QFN, LQFP and friends),
  which are industry-standard mechanical outlines described by the JEDEC/EIAJ standards and the
  vendors' own drawings.

If you intend to redistribute this repository, check WCH's terms for the vendor material first.
The application and its data are separate from it and are MIT.
